    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "A detached home that is going to both charm and impress. This is a high spec property which must be taken seriously as a really quality place to live.\n\nTullagee is a rural countryside area situated just outside Dundalk, in the Knockbridge area. It`s surrounded by rolling countryside, a lovely, quiet place to live. And the property itself enjoys a wonderful private spot within this lovely countryside area.\n\nDundalk train station and Dundalk town centre, with full array of schools and shops, sports and social amenities, are a 12-15 minute drive away. Dublin Airport is about an hour`s drive away, and there are hourly routes by road and rail to Dublin city centre. Dundalk Institute of Technology (which is soon to become a university), will also be an important consideration for many buyers looking to live within the M1 corridor (https://www.m1corridor.ie/). \n\nThe property itself occupies a site of circa 1.14 acres, and it is really well laid out to include:\n- a beautifully horse-railed paddock for horses\n- 2 stables, with separate feed house & hay shed\n- a separate insulated tack room\n- a separate, detached, block-built garage with mezzanine storage\n- a really impressive executive home with impeccably presented accommodation \n\nThe property has been constructed to a very high degree in terms of specification, consideration, and quality. For example, it has underfloor heating throughout, which is powered by geothermal heating. That`s one of the reasons that it commands an A rating, so it`s got very strong energy credentials.\n\nThe accommodation is very well laid out across a ground floor and first floor, plus an important bonus attic conversion for a fantastic, spacious and bright games room. All of the rooms are immaculately presented, extremely well proportioned, and require no effort for its next owner beyond simply moving in and enjoying each space.\n\nWe`re now on the market with this property.\n"
      },
